.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-REPORT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-report
.Nd check a capsule and write a report of it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis report
.Op Fl p | Fl -pub Ar key.pub
.Op Fl f | Fl -format Cm md | txt
.Op Fl o | Fl -out Ar file
.Op Fl j | Fl -json
.Op Fl -github
.Ar dir
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis report
checks the capsule in
.Ar dir
as
.Xr noqtis-check 1
does and its data record as
.Cm noqtis data check
does, once, and writes a report of both
.Pq Xr nqdrpt 3 :
whether every check passed and how many failed, each check of the
capsule, then what the record says of the data (sources, schemas, drift
summaries, environment, steps, recorded checks, commitments, citation)
and each check of the record, named
.Ql data. Ns Ar check .
A folder that is not sealed fails: its report says so in place of the
capsule's checks.
.Pp
In Markdown, a value from the record never breaks its line or its table
cell: a line break in it is a space, and each character Markdown could
read as markup
.Pq Ql "\e \(ga * _ [ ] < > | # ~ & !"
gets one backslash before it.
In plain text a line break is a space too, and nothing else changes.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p , Fl -pub Ar key.pub
the key the seal must carry, as for
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ;
without it, the key inside the seal is trusted
.It Fl f , Fl -format Cm md | txt
Markdown (the default) or plain text
.It Fl o , Fl -out Ar file
write the report to
.Ar file
instead of standard output
.It Fl j , Fl -json
print, instead of the report (which
.Fl o
still writes), one line of JSON:
.Bd -literal
{"capsule":"<dir>","ok":<bool>,"status":"passed"|"failed",
 "sealed":<bool>,"total":<n>,"failed":<n>,"verified":<n>,
 "changed":<n>,"checks":[{"check":"<name>","ok":<bool>,
 "detail":"<text>"},...]}
.Ed
.Pp
.Cm verified
counts the sealed files that match, and
.Cm changed
those changed or missing and the files added since the seal.
.It Fl -github
first print, for each failed check, a GitHub Actions workflow command
.Pp
.Dl ::error title=noqtis <check>::<dir>: <detail>
.Pp
with
.Ql % ,
carriage return and line feed (and in the title
.Ql \&:
and
.Ql \&, )
written as
.Ql %25 ,
.Ql %0D ,
.Ql %0A ,
.Ql %3A
and
.Ql %2C
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
every check passed
.It 1
a check failed, or the folder is not sealed
.It 2
a usage or file error, or a folder with neither a seal nor a data record
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis report -p release.pub -o report.md results
$ noqtis report -f txt results | head -3
noqtis report: results
Passed: 0 of 27 checks failed
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 1 ,
.Xr nqdrpt 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
